vantage.\nStrategic Recommendations: To maximize its market potential, SecurityForce should focus on building industry relationships, implementing targeted marketing strategies, offering free trials, and investing in R&D. Emphasizing user education through webinars and workshops will enhance product value and user engagement.\nUser Feedback and Improvements: User feedback highlights SecurityForce's intuitive interface and accurate threat detection as key strengths. Ongoing improvements should focus on enhancing these features while addressing any identified user pain points. Regular updates and feature enhancements will ensure the product remains at the forefront of API security.\nConclusion: SecurityForce is poised to transform API security with its AI-driven solutions. By addressing the growing demand for robust API security in emerging markets and continuously innovating to meet evolving threats, SecurityForce can establish itself as a leader in the API security market.\nTitle: Revert PR# 6: Scheduling Feature Implementation\nAuthor: eid_f12eccf0\nCreated At: 2026-06-13T20:22:00\nState: closed\nMergeable: True\nMerged: True\nLink: https://github.com/salesforce/ortAIX/pull/8\nSummary: This revert is necessary due to a change in product direction. The focus has shifted towards enhancing existing features rather than adding new ones, and the scheduling feature implemented in PR# 6 no longer aligns with our current priorities. The changes were mostly isolated to the UI, and a dependency check is being conducted to ensure no other parts of the system are affected.\n\nReviews:\n- APPROVED by eid_71e8aec1 at 2026-06-18T15:56:00: LGTM\n- COMMENTED by eid_80cffa39 at 2026-06-18T15:59:00: Looks good\n- COMMENTED by eid_11732422 at 2026-06-18T16:02:00: LGTM\n\nDoc ID: latest_toraix_technical_specifications_document\nLink: https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_toraix_technical_specifications_document\n2026-02-24T21:34:00\nAuthor: eid_4d689aa7\n\nTechnical Specif